VERDICT: FAIL, round 2. One blocking finding (B1). The opus does not close on
this evidence.


ON THE VOIDING OF ROUND 1 — THE STATED REASON IS WRONG

I was handed round 2 on the premise that round 1 "reviewed an unbuilt opus
after a spec-phase stall" and that "its logs were reverted". The tree says
otherwise, and I record that rather than inherit it:

  - studio/ci/W-021-review-1.log is present and committed at 7de09ae. Nothing
    was reverted.
  - It reviewed a built opus. It cites the merged implementation by file, the
    859-test run, the three permitted check.ts edits, the fixture trap, and
    the insurance clause's single firing site. That is not a review of an
    unbuilt opus.

Round 1 has a defect, but a narrower one, and it is the same defect as B1: it
passed the opus while naming the missing reds as "recorded against this opus,
not waived". Naming a gap is not satisfying the evidence contract. A reviewer
cannot waive engineering lex §7 by disclosure; that is the Patron's to waive.
Round 2 therefore reaches the same facts and a different verdict.


